  revision a85b127, are adapted in layastudio/julia.py so Julia checkpoints can be
  fine-tuned in their own format; its weights are downloaded at runtime.

* Decider and decider-ai (https://github.com/Mapika/decider,
  https://huggingface.co/Mapika/decider-2b), Copyright Mark Marosi, licensed under the
  Apache License 2.0. Its prompt layout (decider/prompt.py), its System One adapter
  (decider/systemone.py), its temperature rules (decider/temperature.py) and its training
  loss (decider/train.py, decider/model.py), at commit 45024082, are adapted in
  layastudio/decider.py and layastudio/decider_engine.py; a fine-tune carries the base
  repository's decider/ inference code unchanged. Its weights are downloaded at runtime.

* llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), Copyright the ggml authors, licensed
  under the MIT License. Its converter (convert_hf_to_gguf.py and gguf-py) at commit
  4df29be is downloaded at runtime by layastudio/gguf.py and is not redistributed here.

